00:58:15,580 --> 00:58:17,480
where the hemorrhage
starts within the

1210
00:58:17,480 --> 00:58:19,980
ventricles. That's
usually seen in preterm

1211
00:58:19,980 --> 00:58:22,200
babies where they
have the germinal

1212
00:58:22,200 --> 00:58:24,280
centers within the
ventricles that hemorrhage.

1213
00:58:24,280 --> 00:58:27,050
We'll talk about it
in later lectures.

1214
00:58:27,340 --> 00:58:29,160
Or it could be a
secondary intraventricular

1215
00:58:29,160 --> 00:58:30,960
hemorrhage, which
is usually an

1216
00:58:30,960 --> 00:58:34,060
extension from an
intracerebral hemorrhage.

1217
00:58:34,340 --> 00:58:37,020
And finally, you have
ventriculitis. This

1218
00:58:37,020 --> 00:58:39,620
is the inflammation of
the ependymal cells.

1219
00:58:39,620 --> 00:58:42,420
Those are the special
endothelial cells of

1220
00:58:42,420 --> 00:58:45,060
the choroid plexus that
line the ventricles.

1221
00:58:45,060 --> 00:58:47,050
And you can see the
white enhancement,

1222
00:58:47,050 --> 00:58:50,520
which is from the edema
from the inflammation,

1223
00:58:50,520 --> 00:58:54,040
and this can be from
an infection or a post

1224
00:58:54,040 --> 00:58:56,320
-traumatic or implant
-related meningitis.

1225
00:58:57,880 --> 00:59:00,360
The final pathology
of the ventricular

1226
00:59:00,360 --> 00:59:02,870
system that we'll talk
about is hydrocephalus,

1227
00:59:02,870 --> 00:59:04,840
which is basically
an abnormal

1228
00:59:04,840 --> 00:59:07,380
accumulation of the CSF
within the ventricles

1229
00:59:07,380 --> 00:59:09,700
of the brain, and
there are two primary

1230
00:59:09,700 --> 00:59:12,640
mechanisms by which
this can happen. One is

1231
00:59:12,640 --> 00:59:14,220
because there is
a problem with the

1232
00:59:14,220 --> 00:59:18,080
absorption of CSF from
the ventricular system.

1233
00:59:18,080 --> 00:59:20,820
And the other one
is there's an actual

1234
00:59:21,140 --> 00:59:23,500
overproduction
of CSF. So either

1235
00:59:23,500 --> 00:59:26,140
problem with absorbing
it or a problem

1236
00:59:26,140 --> 00:59:28,220
with too much CSF
overproduction.

1237
00:59:28,220 --> 00:59:29,380
And we already
talked about the

1238
00:59:29,380 --> 00:59:32,160
overproduction, which
only makes up very

1239
00:59:32,960 --> 00:59:36,260
smaller cases of the
hydrocephalus. And it

1240
00:59:36,260 --> 00:59:38,120
can be from the choroid
plexus papilloma,

1241
00:59:38,120 --> 00:59:39,960
which we talked about
in the last slide. So

1242
00:59:39,960 --> 00:59:42,980
mostly hydrocephalus
is caused by subnormal

1243
00:59:42,980 --> 00:59:46,020
CSF reabsorption. And
this can happen by

1244
00:59:46,020 --> 00:59:48,300
two mechanisms.
There's the obstructive

1245
00:59:48,300 --> 00:59:50,260
hydrocephalus, which
is actually, there's a

1246
00:59:50,260 --> 00:59:53,380
mechanical obstruction of
the flow of CSF through

1247
00:59:53,380 --> 00:59:54,840
the ventricular
system that we talked

1248
00:59:54,840 --> 00:59:58,360
about. And the other
one is there's an actual

1249
01:00:00,080 --> 01:00:03,040
problem that's blocking
the reabsorption

1250
01:00:03,040 --> 01:00:06,660
of CSF from the
subarachnoid space into the

1251
01:00:06,660 --> 01:00:08,860
venous system. So
with the obstructive

1252
01:00:08,860 --> 01:00:11,380
hydrocephalus, you
usually observe it,

1253
01:00:11,650 --> 01:00:13,740
obstruction of the sylvian
duct. We talked about

1254
01:00:13,740 --> 01:00:15,260
how the sylvian duct
is the narrowest

1255
01:00:15,260 --> 01:00:17,660
portion in the
ventricular system. So if

1256
01:00:17,660 --> 01:00:20,000
there is any clot or
any mass or anything,

1257
01:00:20,000 --> 01:00:22,320
any tumor, intraventricular
hemorrhage,

1258
01:00:22,320 --> 01:00:25,040
anything like that, that
blocks the flow, then

1259
01:00:25,040 --> 01:00:28,780
you have proximal to
the blockage, you'll

1260
01:00:28,780 --> 01:00:30,760
have ventriculomegaly
and hydrocephalus

1261
01:00:30,760 --> 01:00:33,680
and distilled to the
blockage of wherever

1262
01:00:33,680 --> 01:00:35,760
it is in the ventricular
system, you'll have

1263
01:00:35,760 --> 01:00:39,120
actually smaller
ventricles. So here on

1264
01:00:39,120 --> 01:00:41,960
the MRI, this is a T1
-weighted MRI. Again,

1265
01:00:41,960 --> 01:00:43,910
I know this is T1
-weighted because the

1266
01:00:43,910 --> 01:00:47,280
CSF in the ventricles
are black. If it was

1267
01:00:47,280 --> 01:00:49,280
white, then it would
be a T2-weighted MRI.

1268
01:00:49,640 --> 01:00:52,180
I know I keep talking
about this. This

1269
01:00:52,180 --> 01:00:53,820
is just so that you
guys get used to it.

1270
01:00:54,420 --> 01:00:57,260
So you actually have
a colloid cyst that's

1271
01:00:57,260 --> 01:00:59,280
blocking the
intraventricular foramen,

1272
01:00:59,280 --> 01:01:00,840
which connects your
lateral ventricle into

1273
01:01:00,840 --> 01:01:02,620
the third ventricle,
and what you end up

1274
01:01:02,620 --> 01:01:04,560
having is the
ventriculomegaly of the

1275
01:01:04,560 --> 01:01:06,640
lateral ventricles. So
this is an obstructive

1276
01:01:06,640 --> 01:01:09,080
hydrocephalus, aka
non-communicating

1277
01:01:09,080 --> 01:01:11,940
hydrocephalus. In a
communicating hydrocephalus

1278
01:01:11,940 --> 01:01:14,620
or non-obstructive
hydrocephalus, the

1279
01:01:14,620 --> 01:01:16,680
problem usually lies
within the arachnoid

1280
01:01:16,680 --> 01:01:18,840
villi or the arachnoid
granulation. So

1281
01:01:18,840 --> 01:01:21,320
there's something
obstructing it or that has

1282
01:01:21,320 --> 01:01:24,000
destroyed the arachnoid
granulation so that

1283
01:01:24,000 --> 01:01:26,380
the CSF cannot be
reabsorbed from the

1284
01:01:26,380 --> 01:01:28,640
subarachnoid space
into the venous system.

1285
01:01:28,860 --> 01:01:32,480
And this usually
happens with meningitis

1286
01:01:32,480 --> 01:01:34,760
trauma or subarachnoid
hemorrhage. So

1287
01:01:34,760 --> 01:01:37,160
in this picture,
again, a T1-rated MRI,

1288
01:01:37,160 --> 01:01:39,140
this is a patient
who had subarachnoid

1289
01:01:39,140 --> 01:01:42,180
hemorrhage and then later
on started developing

1290
01:01:42,180 --> 01:01:44,300
hydrocephalus,
which is a common

1291
01:01:44,300 --> 01:01:46,100
complication of
subarachnoid hemorrhage. And

1292
01:01:46,100 --> 01:01:48,120
you can see dilation
of the lateral

1293
01:01:48,120 --> 01:01:50,500
ventricles. And I want
you guys to pay attention.

1294
01:01:50,500 --> 01:01:52,400
You're seeing the
temporal horns of

1295
01:01:52,400 --> 01:01:54,100
the lateral ventricle.
I mentioned that

1296
01:01:54,100 --> 01:01:55,780
usually you don't see
the temporal horns.

1297
01:01:55,780 --> 01:01:58,680
And if you do, that is
a sign of hydrocephalus

1298
01:01:58,680 --> 01:02:00,140
and ventriculomegaly.
And you can

1299
01:02:00,140 --> 01:02:03,280
also see dilation of
the third ventricle.

1300
01:02:03,560 --> 01:02:07,280
And this is probably
due to the blood

1301
01:02:07,280 --> 01:02:10,300
in this subarachnoid
space that probably

1302
01:02:10,300 --> 01:02:12,940
either obstructed
the arachnoid

1303
01:02:12,940 --> 01:02:16,260
granulation or
completely destroyed it.

1304
01:02:18,340 --> 01:02:21,480
And finally, I just
want to mention some

1305
01:02:21,480 --> 01:02:24,440
other miscellaneous
pathologies that result

1306
01:02:24,440 --> 01:02:27,460
in hydrocephalus,
none of which actually

1307
01:02:27,460 --> 01:02:29,220
kind of goes with
the two mechanisms of

1308
01:02:29,220 --> 01:02:31,340
hydrocephalus that I
mentioned in the last

1309
01:02:31,340 --> 01:02:34,040
slide. So we have what's
called the hydrocephalus

1310
01:02:34,040 --> 01:02:36,280
X vacuole. So in
this picture on the

1311
01:02:36,280 --> 01:02:39,040
right, again, T1 rated
MRI, you see that

1312
01:02:39,860 --> 01:02:42,240
ventriculomegaly. But
this is not actually

1313
01:02:42,240 --> 01:02:44,400
due to there's an
overproduction of CSF

1314
01:02:44,400 --> 01:02:46,540
or problem with the
reabsorption. This is

1315
01:02:46,540 --> 01:02:49,000
actually because there
is the atrophy of the

1316
01:02:49,000 --> 01:02:52,080
brain that then
makes the ventricles

1317
01:02:52,080 --> 01:02:54,460
bigger. So it looks like
there's ventriculomegaly

1318
01:02:54,460 --> 01:02:56,780
and you often see
that with Alzheimer's

1319
01:02:56,780 --> 01:02:59,580
patients. There's
the cortical atrophy.

1320
01:02:59,760 --> 01:03:02,820
And another pathology
is called normal

1321
01:03:02,820 --> 01:03:05,420
pressure hydrocephalus
or NPH, a

1322
01:03:05,420 --> 01:03:07,080
heavily tested
topic on the boards.

1323
01:03:07,280 --> 01:03:09,280
This is the actual
mechanism of

1324
01:03:09,280 --> 01:03:11,620
hydrocephalus, not
fully understood, but

1325
01:03:11,620 --> 01:03:13,580
usually when you have
hydrocephalus, you

1326
01:03:13,580 --> 01:03:15,780
have buildup of CSF,
which then causes

1327
01:03:15,780 --> 01:03:18,100
high intracranial
pressure and patients

1328
01:03:18,100 --> 01:03:20,860
usually have
symptoms of high ICP.

1329
01:03:20,860 --> 01:03:23,760
But with NPH, the
pressure is normal,

1330
01:03:23,780 --> 01:03:28,120
and this is often seen
in older adults and

1331
01:03:28,120 --> 01:03:31,260
comes with a triad of
urinary incontinence,

1332
01:03:31,620 --> 01:03:33,260
cognitive dysfunction,

1333
01:03:33,260 --> 01:03:34,820
and gait abnormality,

1334
01:03:34,820 --> 01:03:38,820
often known as wet,
walkie, and wobbly.

1335
01:03:39,140 --> 01:03:42,630
And finally, you have
a pathology called

1336
01:03:42,630 --> 01:03:44,780
pseudotumor cerebris,
which is seen

1337
01:03:44,780 --> 01:03:46,960
in young females.
It's also known as

1338
01:03:46,960 --> 01:03:49,080
idiopathic intracranial
hypertension.

1339
01:03:49,080 --> 01:03:53,580
Again, the actual
mechanism is not fully

1340
01:03:53,580 --> 01:03:55,940
understood, but this is,
again, a hydrocephalus

1341
01:03:55,940 --> 01:03:57,560
that results in
high intracranial

1342
01:03:57,560 --> 01:04:00,460
pressure without an
identifiable mass or

1343
01:04:00,460 --> 01:04:02,880
obstruction in the brain.
And the patients usually

1344
01:04:02,880 --> 01:04:05,220
complain of classic
headache, transient

1345
01:04:05,220 --> 01:04:08,040
visual loss, pulsatile
tinnitus, and

1346
01:04:08,040 --> 01:04:12,200
dizziness. And the
management usually depends

1347
01:04:13,080 --> 01:04:17,120
on draining the CSF
using a lumbar drain.

1348
01:04:17,120 --> 01:04:19,470
So you're trying to
relieve that intracranial

1349
01:04:19,470 --> 01:04:21,580
pressure by taking
out some of the CSF.

